Cell["", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[TextData[{
    "Corollary ",
    
    CounterBox["Section"],
    ".",
    
    CounterBox["Theorem"],
    ". "
  }], "CorollaryLabel",
    TaggingRules:>{"CellLabel" -> True}],
  "Suppose ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalX]\)]],
  " is a Grothendieck topos and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`F : \[ScriptCapitalE] \[Rule] \[ScriptCapitalX]\)]],
  " is a dense, fully faithful, left exact functor. Then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`F\)]],
  " preserves internal ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  "-products for any powerful ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  "."
}], "Corollary",
  TaggingRules:>{"ExtraConversionRules" -> {"General" -> {"RestartList" -> 
    True}}},
  ParagraphIndent->0,
  CounterIncrements->"Theorem",
  CellTags->"XRef-Corollary-51818382"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof.",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`F\)]],
  " is dense, the functor ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{\(\(F\&~\) : \[ScriptCapitalX]\), "\[Rule]", 
          RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{\(\[ScriptCapitalE]\^op\), ",", 
              StyleBox["Set",
                FontWeight->"Bold"]}], 
            StyleBox["]",
              FontWeight->"Plain"]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " defined by ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(F\&~\) X = \[ScriptCapitalX](\(\(F\)\(-\)\), 
          X)\)]],
  " is fully faithful. Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`F\)]],
  " is fully faithful, the composite ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          FormBox[\(F\&~\),
            "TraditionalForm"], " ", "F"}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " is isomorphic to the Yoneda embedding ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptY]\_\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ". Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`F\)]],
  " is left exact and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalX]\)]],
  " is a Grothendieck topos, the functor ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`F\&~\)]],
  " has a left exact left adjoint. Hence the conditions of Proposition ",
  ButtonBox[
  CounterBox["Section", "XRef-Proposition-518185647"],
    ButtonData:>{"Counter" -> "Theorem", "CounterTag" -> 
      "XRef-Proposition-518185647"},
    ButtonStyle->"XRef"],
  StyleBox[".", "Nil"],
  StyleBox[
  CounterBox["Theorem", "XRef-Proposition-518185647"], "Nil"],
  "\[InvisibleSpace] apply to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`T = F\&~\)]],
  " and therefore we have ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{\(F\&~\_\(F\ B\)\), 
            SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], \(F\ p\)]}], "\[TildeFullEqual]", 
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
                
                FontSlant->
                  "Plain"], \(\[ScriptY]\_\[ScriptCapitalE]\ p\)], \
\(F\&~\_\(F\ E\)\)}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ". By Proposition ",
  ButtonBox[
  CounterBox["Section", "XRef-Proposition-51819521"],
    ButtonData:>{"Counter" -> "Theorem", "CounterTag" -> 
      "XRef-Proposition-51819521"},
    ButtonStyle->"XRef"],
  StyleBox[".", "Nil"],
  StyleBox[
  CounterBox["Theorem", "XRef-Proposition-51819521"], "Nil"],
  "\[InvisibleSpace] we consequently have   "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell[BoxData[
    FormBox[
      RowBox[{
        RowBox[{\(F\&~\_\(F\ B\)\), \(F\_B\), 
          SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], "p"]}], "\[TildeFullEqual]", 
        RowBox[{\(\((\[ScriptY]\_\[ScriptCapitalE])\)\_B\), 
          SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], "p"]}], "\[TildeFullEqual]", 
        SubscriptBox[
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], \(\[ScriptY]\_\[ScriptCapitalE]\ p\)], 
            "(", \(\[ScriptY]\_\[ScriptCapitalE]\), ")"}], "E"], 
        "\[TildeFullEqual]", 
        RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
              
              FontSlant->
                "Plain"], \(\[ScriptY]\_\[ScriptCapitalE]\ p\)], \(F\&~\_\(F\ \
E\)\), \(F\_E\)}], "\[TildeFullEqual]", 
        RowBox[{\(F\&~\_\(F\ B\)\), 
          SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], \(F\ p\)], \(\(F\_E\)\(\ \ \)\(.\)\)}]}], 
      TraditionalForm]], "Equation"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`F\&~\_\(F\ B\)\)]],
  " is fully faithful, we conclude the required ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{\(F\_B\), 
            SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], "p"]}], "\[TildeFullEqual]", 
          RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["\[CapitalPi]",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], \(F\ p\)], \(F\_E\)}]}], 
        TraditionalForm]]],
  ".     ",
  StyleBox["\[EmptySquare]", "QED"],
  "       "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell["", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We are interested in finding some powerful morphisms in a functor category \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        StyleBox[\([\[ScriptCapitalC], \[ScriptCapitalE]]\),
          FontSlant->"Plain"], TraditionalForm]]],
  " in terms of those in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ". We are grateful to Steve Lack for vastly simplifying our proof of:"
}], "Text"],

Cell["", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[TextData[{
    "Theorem ",
    
    CounterBox["Section"],
    ".",
    
    CounterBox["Theorem"],
    ". "
  }], "TheoremLabel",
    TaggingRules:>{"CellLabel" -> True}],
  "Suppose ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalC]\)]],
  " is a category and suppose ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  " has products indexed by the set ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalC]\_1\)],
    Editable->True],
  " of morphisms of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalC]\)],
    Editable->True],
  ". A morphism ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p : E \[Rule] B\)]],
  " in the functor category ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        StyleBox[\([\[ScriptCapitalC], \[ScriptCapitalE]]\),
          FontSlant->"Plain"], TraditionalForm]]],
  " is powerful if it is componentwise powerful; that is, for all objects ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`U \[Element] \[ScriptCapitalC]\)]],
  ", the component ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(p\_U\) : E\ U \[Rule] B\ U\)]],
  " is powerful in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ". "
}], "Theorem",
  TaggingRules:>{"ExtraConversionRules" -> {"General" -> {"RestartList" -> 
    True}}},
  ParagraphIndent->0,
  CounterIncrements->"Theorem",
  CellTags->"XRef-Theorem-427112141"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof\[InvisibleSpace]. ",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  "Let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`J : \[ScriptCapitalC]\_0 \[Rule] \
\[ScriptCapitalC]\)]],
  " denote the inclusion of the set of objects ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalC]\_0\)]],
  " as a discrete category. The hypothesis of the first sentence is used to \
obtain the functor "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(TraditionalForm\`R : \([\[ScriptCapitalC]\_0, \[ScriptCapitalE]]\)\
\[LongRightArrow]\([\[ScriptCapitalC], \[ScriptCapitalE]]\), \ \ \ \ \(R(T)\) 
        U = \[Product]\+\(V \[Element] \[ScriptCapitalC]\_0\)\((T\ V)\)\^\(\
\[ScriptCapitalC](U, V)\), \)], "EquationNumbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "which is right Kan extension along ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`J\)]],
  ". Consider the following square of functors."
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell[BoxData[
    FormBox[GridBox[{
          {\(\([\[ScriptCapitalC], \[ScriptCapitalE]]\)\_\(\(/\)\(B\)\)\), \(\
\[LongRightArrow]\&\(p\^\[Star]\)\), \(\([\[ScriptCapitalC], \
\[ScriptCapitalE]]\)\_\(\(/\)\(E\)\)\)},
          {\(\(\[InvisiblePrefixScriptBase]\^\([J, 1]\)\_B\)\[DownArrow]\), 
            "\[TildeFullEqual]", \(\[DownArrow]\^\([J, 1]\)\_E\)},
          {\(\([\[ScriptCapitalC]\_0, \[ScriptCapitalE]]\)\_\(\(\(/\)\(B\)\)\ \
J\)\), 
            UnderscriptBox["\[LongRightArrow]", 
              StyleBox[\(\((p\ J)\)\^\[Star]\),
                
                Editable->
                  True]], \(\([\[ScriptCapitalC]\_0, \[ScriptCapitalE]]\)\_\(\
\(\(/\)\(E\)\)\ J\)\)}
          }], TraditionalForm]], "EquationNumbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The vertical functors are comonadic with right adjoints easily obtained \
from ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " and pullback along the unit. In particular, the units of the adjunctions \
are pointwise regular monomorphisms. The bottom functor has a right adjoint \
precisely because each component ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(p\_U\) : E\ U \[Rule] B\ U\)]],
  " is powerful in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ". So Lemma ",
  ButtonBox[
  CounterBox["Section", "XRef-Lemma-51616391"],
    ButtonData:>{"Counter" -> "Theorem", "CounterTag" -> 
      "XRef-Lemma-51616391"},
    ButtonStyle->"XRef"],
  StyleBox[".", "Nil"],
  StyleBox[
  CounterBox["Theorem", "XRef-Lemma-51616391"], "Nil"],
  "\[InvisibleSpace] applies to yield a right adjoint for the top functor. So \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p : E \[Rule] B\)]],
  " is powerful",
  ".     ",
  StyleBox["\[EmptySquare]", "QED"]
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell["", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[TextData[{
    "Theorem ",
    
    CounterBox["Section"],
    ".",
    
    CounterBox["Theorem"],
    ". "
  }], "TheoremLabel",
    TaggingRules:>{"CellLabel" -> True}],
  "In the situation of Theorem ",
