  "  "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell["", "TextContinuation"],

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[TextData[{
    "Proposition ",
    
    CounterBox["Section"],
    ".",
    
    CounterBox["Theorem"],
    ". "
  }], "PropositionLabel",
    TaggingRules:>{"CellLabel" -> True}],
  "Each final discrete fibration into an amenable object is invertible."
}], "Proposition",
  TaggingRules:>{"ExtraConversionRules" -> {"General" -> {"RestartList" -> 
    True}}},
  ParagraphIndent->0,
  CounterIncrements->"Theorem",
  CellTags->"XRef-Proposition-59121852"],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof.",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " Suppose ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p : E \[Rule] B\)]],
  " is a final discrete fibration with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`B\)]],
  " amenable. Let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`i : B\_0 \[Rule] B\)]],
  " be the inclusion. Then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(d\_1\) : \((i/B)\) \[Rule] B\)]],
  " is a powerful discrete opfibration by Corollary ",
  ButtonBox[
  CounterBox["Section", "XRef-Corollary-55155743"],
    ButtonData:>{"Counter" -> "Theorem", "CounterTag" -> 
      "XRef-Corollary-55155743"},
    ButtonStyle->"XRef"],
  StyleBox[".", "Nil"],
  StyleBox[
  CounterBox["Theorem", "XRef-Corollary-55155743"], "Nil"],
  "\[InvisibleSpace]. So the pullback ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`g : \((i/p)\) \[Rule] \((i/B)\)\)]],
  " of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " along ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(d\_1\) : \((i/B)\) \[Rule] B\)]],
  " is inverted by ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Pi]\_0\)]],
  ". Using Proposition ",
  ButtonBox[
  CounterBox["Section", "XRef-Proposition-5516046"],
    ButtonData:>{"Counter" -> "Theorem", "CounterTag" -> 
      "XRef-Proposition-5516046"},
    ButtonStyle->"XRef"],
  StyleBox[".", "Nil"],
  StyleBox[
  CounterBox["Theorem", "XRef-Proposition-5516046"], "Nil"],
  "\[InvisibleSpace], we see that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\[Pi]\_0\)(g)\)]],
  " is isomorphic to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(p\_0\) : E\_0 \[Rule] B\_0\)]],
  ". A discrete fibration ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\_0\)]],
  " invertible is clearly invertible.     ",
  StyleBox["\[EmptySquare]", "QED"],
  "   "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell["", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[TextData[{
    "Proposition ",
    
    CounterBox["Section"],
    ".",
    
    CounterBox["Theorem"],
    ". "
  }], "PropositionLabel",
    TaggingRules:>{"CellLabel" -> True}],
  "If ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`B\)]],
  " is amenable then the category ",
