Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Torsors", "Section"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  " denote a finitely complete and let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK] = Cat\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  " be the 2-category of categories in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "A discrete fibration ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p : E \[Rule] B\)]],
  " in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK]\)]],
  " is said to be ",
  StyleBox["representable",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " when there exist a morphism ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x : 1 \[Rule] B\)]],
  " and an isomorphism ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((B/x)\) \[TildeFullEqual] E\)]],
  " over ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`B\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Suppose ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p : E \[Rule] B\)]],
  " is a discrete fibration in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK]\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " is an object of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ". Then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\[Cross]\(R : E\[Cross]R\) \[Rule] B\[Cross]R\)]],
  " is a discrete fibration in the 2-category ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK]\_\(\(/\)\(R\)\)\)]],
  " of categories in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\_\(\(/\)\(R\)\)\)]],
  ". When ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\[Cross]\(R : E\[Cross]R\) \[Rule] B\[Cross]R\)]],
  " is representable, one says ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " is ",
  StyleBox["representable over ",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  ". "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Suppose ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`B\)]],
  " is a category in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ". A ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`B\)]],
  StyleBox["-torsor",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " is a discrete fibration ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p : E \[Rule] B\)]],
  " in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK]\)]],
  " for which there exists an object ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  " with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R \[Rule] 1\)]],
  " a regular epimorphism and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " representable over ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  ". "
}], "Text"],

Cell["", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[TextData[{
    "Proposition ",
    
    CounterBox["Section"],
    ".",
    
    CounterBox["Theorem"],
    ". "
  }], "PropositionLabel",
    TaggingRules:>{"CellLabel" -> True}],
  "The following conditions on a discrete fibration ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p : E \[Rule] B\)]],
  " and an object ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  " are equivalent:"
}], "Proposition",
  TaggingRules:>{"ExtraConversionRules" -> {"General" -> {"RestartList" -> 
    True}}},
  ParagraphIndent->0,
  CounterIncrements->"Theorem",
  CellTags->"XRef-Proposition-59163410"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "the discrete fibration ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " is representable over ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  ";"
}], "EnunciationItem3Numbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "there exists a morphism ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y : R \[Rule] E\)]],
  " and a 2-cell ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi] : 
          pr\_1 \[Implies] y\ \(\(pr\_2\) : E\[Cross]R\) \[Rule] E\)]],
  " whose restriction along ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((y, 1)\) : R \[Rule] E\[Cross]R\)]],
  " is the identity 2-cell of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y\)]],
  "; \[InvisibleSpace]"
}], "EnunciationItem3Numbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "the category ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK](R, E)\)]],
  " has a terminal object which is preserved by composition with all ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`u : R\^\[Prime] \[Rule] R\)]],
  " in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ";"
}], "EnunciationItem3Numbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "(for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " powerful in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ") the morphism ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`E\^R \[Rule] 1\)]],
  " in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK]\)]],
  " has a right adjoint."
}], "EnunciationItem3Numbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Furthermore, the pair ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((y, \[Chi])\)\)]],
  " is unique up to isomorphism when it exists."
}], "PropositionContinuation"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof.",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " To say that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " is representable over ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " is to say that there exists ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x : R \[Rule] B\)]],
  " and a morphism of spans "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(TraditionalForm\`t : \((d\_0, \((B/x)\), 
          d\_1)\)\[LongRightArrow]\((p\ pr\_1, E\[Cross]R, 
          R)\)\)], "EquationNumbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "from ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`B\)]],
  " with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\)]],
  " invertible. By Yoneda\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Lemma in a 2-category, morphisms \
of spans ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\)]],
  " are in bijection with morphisms of spans"
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(TraditionalForm\`k : \(\(\((x, R, 1)\)\[LongRightArrow]\((p\ pr\_1, 
            E\[Cross]R, pr\_2)\)\)\(\ \)\(.\)\)\)], "EquationNumbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Such a ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`k\)]],
  " must have the form ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`k = \((y, 1)\)\)]],
  " for a unique ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y\)]],
  " with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\ y = x\)]],
  ". On the other hand, morphisms of spans "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(TraditionalForm\`\(t\^\[Prime]\) : \((p\ pr\_1, E\[Cross]R, 
          R)\)\[LongRightArrow]\((d\_0, \((B/x)\), 
          d\_1)\)\)], "EquationNumbered"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "are in bijection with 2-cells ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Mu] : 
          p\ pr\_1 \[Implies] x\ \(\(pr\_2\) : E\[Cross]R\) \[Rule] B\)]],
  " via the universal property of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((B/x)\)\)]],
  ". Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " is a discrete fibration, there exists a unique 2-cell ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi]\)]],
  " with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\ \[Chi] = \[Mu]\)]],
  ". The condition ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\ t\^\[Prime] = 1\)]],
  " becomes ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(pr\_1\) t\ t\^\[Prime] = pr\_1\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(pr\_2\) t\ t\^\[Prime] = pr\_2\)]],
  ". The second of these is automatic while the first means that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi]\)]],
  " has domain ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`pr\_1\)]],
  ". The condition ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(t\^\[Prime]\) t = 1\)]],
  " becomes ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Mu]\ \((y, 1)\) = 1\_x\)]],
  " which amounts to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi]\ \((y, 1)\) = 1\_y\)]],
  " since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p\)]],
  " is discrete. This proves (i)\[DoubleLeftRightArrow](ii).   "
}], "TextContinuation"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Assuming (ii), we easily see that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y\ u\)]],
  " is terminal in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK](R\^\[Prime], E)\)]],
  " which gives (iii). "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "It is easy to see that (iv) amounts to saying that there exists ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y : R \[Rule] E\)]],
  " such that, for all ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`X\)]],
  " in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalE]\)]],
  ", the composite ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y\ \(\(pr\_2\) : X\[Cross]R\) \[Rule] E\)]],
  " is terminal in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK](X\[Cross]R, E)\)]],
  ". So certainly (iii)\[Implies](iv). Yet (iv) easily implies that, for all \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`A\)]],
  " in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK]\)]],
  ", the composite ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y\ \(\(pr\_2\) : A\[Cross]R\) \[Rule] E\)]],
  " is terminal in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalK](A\[Cross]R, E)\)]],
  ". With ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`A = E\)]],
  ", there is therefore a unique ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi] : 
          pr\_1 \[Implies] y\ \(\(pr\_2\) : E\[Cross]R\) \[Rule] E\)]],
  ". With ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`X = 1\)]],
  ", we see that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y\)]],
  " has only one endomorphism; so ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi]\ \((y, 1)\) = 1\)]],
  ". So (iv)\[Implies](ii)",
  ".       ",
  StyleBox["\[EmptySquare]", "QED"],
  "      "
}], "Text"],

Cell["", "Text"],

