Cell[TextData[{
  StyleBox["Proof.",
    FontSlant->"Italic"],
  " Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`X\[Cross]-\)]],
  " preserves coequalizers, if ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\^\[Prime]\)]],
  " are in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[ScriptCapitalR]\)]],
  ", so is ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\[Cross]R\^\[Prime]\)]],
  ". This proves the first sentence. There is a unique 2-cell ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Chi] : 
          pr\_1 \[Implies] u\ \(\(pr\_2\) : R\_c\[Cross]R\^\[Prime]\) \[Rule] 
        R\_c\)]],
  " which (by Proposition ",
